{"title":"1981 USAMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Show that for any positive real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/0/890ce23466abfd1bcb2eb253ac571925c0362163.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[nx]\\ge \\sum_{1}^{n}\\left(\\frac{[kx]}{k}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"141\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution.28due_to_Pavel_Zatitskiy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution(due_to_Pavel_Zatitskiy)\">Solution(due to Pavel Zatitskiy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution(due to Pavel Zatitskiy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First of all we write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/4/0d4a0d2f325f9215668973f735ec2166dba659f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[kx]=kx-\\{kx\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"135\" height=\"19\" />. So, we need to prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/0/63070d2537be3dcacfaed88a7b656bad706fe45b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{1}^{n}\\left(\\frac{\\{kx\\}}{k}\\right)\\geq \\{nx\\}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"164\" height=\"48\" />\nLet's denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/c/79c89a221f82f6f3eacff2e46b5842022e9fc83f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k=\\{kx\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />. It is easy to see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/c/c5cddf94fcfc8887c8b99faed15066d9045af24f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k+a_m \\geq a_{k+m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"16\" />. We need to prove\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/e/2de84014d400959bd26cba554fe483f596339c8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{1}^{n}\\left(\\frac{a_k}{k}\\right)\\geq a_n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"118\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>We will prove it by induction by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. The base is obvious, so we need to make a step.\n</p><p>Let's take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/6/49633d7acb858bc4dcea661a448aa017c00fd745.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a_m}{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"24\" height=\"33\" /> is minimal. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/c/fec4f3da4f422b2346efe86724c8a0aee1023fac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"10\" /> then our inequality is obvious. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/c/3cc5d678e78938bc0ceb0fed5e5694362b69fb36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m&lt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"10\" />. Then, by induction, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/0/a201795e91f3f1ce8c93234f10fce7c643a62cc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{1}^{n-m}\\left(\\frac{a_k}{k}\\right)\\geq a_{n-m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"143\" height=\"55\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/b/f8b5942f9227146fb4abea8b70bb392662add21e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{n-m+1}^{n}\\left(\\frac{a_k}{k}\\right)\\geq m\\cdot \\frac{a_m}{m}=a_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"218\" height=\"49\" />. Now we can add these two inequalities and get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/9/bc999787c9b8a87b1cdb84316d51ccb1ea9fbe7c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{1}^{n}\\left(\\frac{a_k}{k}\\right) \\geq a_{n-m}+a_m \\geq a_n\\]\" width=\"222\" height=\"47\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_USAMO\" title=\"1981 USAMO\">1981 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1981 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1981\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1981 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1981 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1981 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1981 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1981 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017173704\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.049 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 114/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1237/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2946/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.533      1 -total\n 55.49%    6.954      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 42.13%    5.280      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11421:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017